 implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal"],"id":"long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.40 (Last-skip iff local fatality: a pointwise criterion)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.40, p. 55, label thm:last-skip-iff-fatal","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Keep $G$ for the selected half-greedy support, $r_M(1/2)$ for its remainder and $R_M$ for the complete tail after rank $M$. A positive rank $M$ is the last omitted rank if and only if $M\\notin G$ and $r_M(1/2)>R_M$. Consequently,\n$$\n\\frac12\\in\\mathcal A\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n r_M(1/2)\\le R_M\\quad\\text{for every positive }M\\notin G.\n$$\nThus it suffices to check the tail inequality at the ranks actually omitted by the greedy rule. This is an equivalence on that fixed orbit; it does not establish the inequality at its unboundedly many possible omitted ranks.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_iff_every_actual_skip_survives%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.thm-last-skip-iff-fatal%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_iff_every_actual_skip_survives%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.half_mem_iff_every_actual_skip_survives"},{"derive